body.text:
His story is, in many ways, the story of Philippine diplomacy itself:
from post-war emergence to Cold War alignment,
from archipelagic assertion to multilateral leadership,
from bilateral courtesies to the forging of international law.

Because in a world of conflict and uncertainty, someone must carry the flag not in battle,
but in dialogue;
not in conquest,
but in conscience;
not in silence,
but in the steady, principled voice of a people.
